From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 23:37:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform/sky1: guard sky1_power_model_work_handler against
 NULL IPA model

STATUS (2026-07-27): HARDWARE-VALIDATED on real O6N. Booted with this
patch applied (2027+2028 SCMI probe-order fixes also present) and the
sky1_power_model_work_handler/kbase_get_real_power_locked NULL-deref
crash this patch targets did NOT recur — confirmed via full serial
console capture through the boot. mali_kbase now gets past this specific
race cleanly. (A DIFFERENT, unrelated NULL-deref was hit later in the
same boot, in devfreq's clk_round_rate path — see README.md, that is a
separate latent bug this patch does not address.)

Real crash observed on cixmini/O6N with the 2027+2028 SCMI-perf-domain
probe-order fixes applied (those fix the original mali_kbase EPROBE_DEFER
block): once mali_kbase's probe gets far enough to actually run
kbase_platform_sky1_late_init(), its hrtimer immediately queues
sky1_power_model_work_handler(), which calls kbase_get_real_power_locked()
-> get_current_model(). kbase_ipa_init() (which populates
kbdev->ipa.configured_model / kbdev->ipa.fallback_model) runs from
kbase_backend_devfreq_init()/kbase_devfreq_init(), a separate call with
no ordering guarantee relative to platform_late_init_func(). This window
was previously unreachable on this kernel (probe never got past the
"perf" domain attach), so the race was latent and never fired. Root-caused
from a real serial-console crash trace + addr2line against a
debug-symbol build of mali_kbase.ko:

    [    6.945344]   FSC = 0x04: level 0 translation fault
    Workqueue: sky1_power_wq sky1_power_model_work_handler [mali_kbase]
    kbase_get_real_power_locked+0xb0/0x378 [mali_kbase] (P)
    Code: aa0003e1 d2847800 8b0002a0 94000c5e (f9400ac0)

  $ addr2line -e mali_kbase.ko.debug -f -C 0x8ae28
  kbase_get_real_power_locked
  drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/ipa/mali_kbase_ipa.c:679

Line 679 is `err = model->ops->get_dynamic_coeff(model, power_coeffs);`
with `model` NULL (get_current_model() returned
kbdev->ipa.configured_model, still unset). Disassembly confirms: the
faulting instruction `ldr x0, [x22, #16]` reads model->ops with x22 (the
model pointer) loaded a few instructions earlier from kbdev->ipa.*model,
matching exactly.

Fix: skip the sample (rather than trying to fix init ordering, which
risks other regressions) if neither IPA model pointer is populated yet;
the hrtimer re-arms unconditionally and retries next tick once
kbase_ipa_init() has run. Moved get_sky1_static_power() after the guard
since it doesn't need to run on the skip path.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-specific, sky1 platform code]
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/platform/sky1/mali_kbase_config_sky1.c | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/platform/sky1/mali_kbase_config_sky1.c b/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/platform/sky1/mali_kbase_config_sky1.c
index ddda122..9bc8926 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/platform/sky1/mali_kbase_config_sky1.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/platform/sky1/mali_kbase_config_sky1.c
@@ -303,13 +303,38 @@ static void sky1_power_model_work_handler(struct work_struct *work)
 {
 	struct kbase_device *kbdev = container_of(work, struct kbase_device, sky1_power_work);
 	u32 power;
-	u32 static_power = get_sky1_static_power(kbdev);
+	u32 static_power;
 
 	mutex_lock(&kbdev->ipa.lock);
+	/*
+	 * PROPOSED FIX (2026-07-26, NCZ 7.0.12-cix-sky1-next mali_kbase port,
+	 * UNTESTED ON HARDWARE): kbase_ipa_init() -- which populates
+	 * kbdev->ipa.{configured,fallback}_model -- runs from
+	 * kbase_backend_devfreq_init()/kbase_devfreq_init(), called during
+	 * kbase_device_init(). platform_late_init_func() (which starts the
+	 * hrtimer that queues this handler) is a separate, earlier-firing
+	 * hook with no ordering guarantee relative to devfreq/IPA init
+	 * completing first. On 7.0.12-cix-sky1-next this window was
+	 * previously unreachable (sky1_gpu_attach_pd()'s "perf" power-domain
+	 * attach permanently EPROBE_DEFERed before probe ever got this far);
+	 * once that's fixed (see the 2027/2028 kernel patches), this
+	 * handler's very first invocation can race ahead of kbase_ipa_init()
+	 * and call kbase_get_real_power_locked() -> get_current_model() with
+	 * both model pointers still NULL, which NULL-derefs on
+	 * model->ops->get_dynamic_coeff (confirmed via addr2line against a
+	 * real crash: mali_kbase_ipa.c:679, kbase_get_real_power_locked+0xb0).
+	 * Skip this sample if IPA isn't registered yet; the hrtimer re-arms
+	 * unconditionally and will retry on the next tick once it is.
+	 */
+	if (!kbdev->ipa.configured_model && !kbdev->ipa.fallback_model) {
+		mutex_unlock(&kbdev->ipa.lock);
+		return;
+	}
 	kbase_get_real_power_locked(kbdev, &power, kbdev->current_nominal_freq,
 						(kbdev->current_voltages[0] / 1000));
 	mutex_unlock(&kbdev->ipa.lock);
 
+	static_power = get_sky1_static_power(kbdev);
 	if(power > static_power)
 			power -= static_power;
 
--
2.51.0
